$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
[1,1′-Biphenyl]-2-ylcarbamate.17 The product was obtained following the
general procedure (4.0 mmol scale) as yellow solids (916 mg, 85%) after
purification by column chromatography. Rf = 0.29 (5% AcOEt/hexanes); 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.11 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (dd, J = 7.5, 7.5 Hz, 2H),
7.45-7.31 (m, 4H), 7.20 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (t, J = 7.5 Hz,
1H), 6.57-6.45 (br s, 1H), 1.46 (s, 9H).
